  message: "P4 REVIEW 2026-11-01 (dev 9ae4abe13f; owner-requested re-check of open P4 items last modified before 2026-10-20; fixtures under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/p4_review_11012026/langs1/). VERDICT: CURRENT. Reviewed 2026-11-01 on dev 9ae4abe13f. 'type A = int' parses as ERROR(type, ERROR(type_placeholder A, =), int), and no symbol is emitted. 'type Meters = int' parses cleanly as type_declaration and still emits nothing; v_lang.py has no type_declaration branch. Both halves hold. Side finding, not in this item: _recover_single_letter_type also misses 'struct S {}' for the letters C,E,F,G,S,X. For those letters the grammar gives ERROR('struct S') + block with no type_placeholder child, so S is not emitted (A,B,T recover). Worth a sibling item. MECHANISM: tree-sitter-v lexes a lone capital as type_placeholder; recovery covers struct/enum/interface only and the analyzer has no type_declaration (alias) branch."  # 636d
